From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] edgetpu/janeiro: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(edgetpu/janeiro: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/edgetpu/janeiro to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
API migrations. Mostly mechanical; entries that change behaviour say so:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)
  - MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string literal (6.13)
  - iommu_domain_alloc(bus) replaced by iommu_paging_domain_alloc(dev) (6.11)
  - iommu_attach_device_pasid() takes an attach handle (6.11)
  - eventfd_signal() takes only the context (6.8)
  - struct fd: fd_file() accessor (6.12); no_llseek removed (6.12)
  - IOMMU fault reporting moved to the pixel_iommu registry samsung_iommu.ko exports
  - hrtimer_setup(); explicit <linux/vmalloc.h>

Files: drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-device-group.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-dmabuf.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-domain-pool.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-external.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-fs.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-google-iommu.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-mobile-platform.c, drivers/edgetpu/edgetpu-telemetry.c, drivers/edgetpu/janeiro-platform.c, drivers/edgetpu/mobile-firmware.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * dma_fence::lock -> dma_fence_spinlock().
  * thermal_of_cooling_device_register() gained a cdev_id argument (0).

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3; ACK-only interfaces are
handled here rather than restored in the kernel, see kernel/patches/README.md):
  * Kbuild for the ddk_modules here, generated from BUILD.bazel by
    tools/bazel2kbuild.py, for the make-only build (kernel/kbuild.mk):
      drivers/edgetpu/Kbuild
---
